^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-08-24 10:00] observe — VS Code and Neovim already expose shared LSP probes; IntelliJ native LSP provides standard rename but not the custom-request lane.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:01] decide — preserve native LSP rename for caret edits and reserve the CLI refactor command for explicit read-only corpus plans.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:02] taste — command names should transfer between terminal and editor while each editor retains native presentation and cancellation behavior.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:03] decide — use tool-root selection for npm prefix and consumer-root selection for process cwd so mounted infrastructure never takes consumer authority.
 >>[2026-08-24 14:40] implement — added pure Kotlin, TypeScript, and Lua invocation models for form, stack, cache, and plan-only corpus refactoring.
 >>[2026-08-24 14:55] decide — IntelliJ results open as read-only typed preview files; this preserves reusable JSON/Spw output without introducing a persistent tool window before repeated-use evidence exists.
 >>[2026-08-24 14:56] implement — added explicit background IntelliJ actions for saved-file form, stack, cache, native LSP rename, and plan-only corpus refactoring.
}

